# Copy to .env.local for local development.
#
# Settings (URLs, model, timeouts, the local dev user…) live in config/:
# common.ts, plus local.ts or prod.ts. `next dev` and tests run as local,
# production builds and `next start` as prod. This file is only for secrets;
# next.config.ts refuses to start a server that's missing one it needs.

# OpenDashboards' own database (see docker-compose.yml). On Vercel, Neon sets this to
# its pooled URL and DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED to the direct one for migrations.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://opendashboards:opendashboards@localhost:54329/opendashboards

# The gateway sends the user's Supabase access token (Authorization: Bearer)
# on every request. SUPABASE_URL is the project that issues it, required in
# prod. Leave it unset locally to skip the check and act as config/local.ts's
# dev user.
# SUPABASE_URL=

# Secret storage. When KMS_KEY_ID is set, keys are sealed with AWS KMS. Unset
# locally: keys are stored unencrypted, which prod refuses. KMS_ROLE_ARN is the
# role assumed through Vercel OIDC; required in prod.
# KMS_KEY_ID=
# KMS_ROLE_ARN=

# The read-only Neon role every demo dataset (config/common.ts
# demoDatasets) is read through. Required in prod. Unset locally: demo
# datasets aren't offered.
# DEMO_DATABASE_PASSWORD=
